pub sub style thing

00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:19.060
where you can basically push
notifications from the server

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:20.350
side to the browser.

00:22:20.350 --> 00:22:22.790
And their technology makes
that really easy to do.

00:22:22.790 --> 00:22:23.540
MARK MANDEL: Cool.

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:25.206
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah,
very interesting,

00:22:25.206 --> 00:22:28.430
because I know that we have
some-- there's the web--

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:30.430
I think App Engine socket APS--

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:31.770
MARK MANDEL: Channels API.

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:33.210
FRANCESC CAMPOY: That I
have not used that much,

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:34.630
but I was very curious about it.

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:35.300
ANDY OXFELD: Yeah,
we haven't actually

00:22:35.300 --> 00:22:36.674
looked too much
into that either,

00:22:36.674 --> 00:22:39.260
but I do think it is probably
pretty similar to the service

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:40.030
PubNub provides.

00:22:40.030 --> 00:22:41.770
FRANCESC CAMPOY: I was in
between that or Firebase, so

00:22:41.770 --> 00:22:42.340
yeah.

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:43.420
MARK MANDEL: Yeah, yeah.

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:44.200
Excellent.

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:44.700
Cool.

